{"slug": "jicama-and-sun-dried-tomato-salad-with-champagne-vinaigrette", "nyt_id": 6577, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/6577-jicama-and-sun-dried-tomato-salad-with-champagne-vinaigrette", "name": "Jicama-And-Sun-Dried-Tomato Salad With Champagne Vinaigrette", "author": "Molly O’Neill", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "Four servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 75, "raw": {"total": "1 hour 15 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "12 sun-dried tomatoes, julienned", "group": null, "quantity": 12.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "sun-dried tomatoes", "preparation": "julienned", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 tablespoon chopped cilantro", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped cilantro", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "⅓ teaspoon freshly ground black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": 0.3333333333333333, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "freshly ground black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 tablespoon chopped chives", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped chives", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "2 teaspoons lime juice", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "lime juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 tablespoon lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 teaspoon olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "3 tablespoons Champagne vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "champagne vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "2 ⅔ cups julienned jicama, placed in a bowl of cold water and refrigerated", "group": null, "quantity": 2.6666666666666665, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "julienned jicama", "preparation": "placed in a bowl of cold water and refrigerated", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 cup finely shredded radicchio", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "finely shredded radicchio", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "1 tablespoon lime zest", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "lime zest", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "In a small bowl combine tomatoes, cilantro, pepper, chives, lime and lemon juice, olive oil and vinegar. Refrigerate at least 1 hour. Drain jicama and toss with tomato mixture. Place ¼ cup of the radicchio on each of 4 plates. Arrange a heaping ½ cup of the salad over the radicchio. Garnish with lime zest and serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 65.6, "protein_g": 1.7, "carbohydrates_g": 12.3, "fat_g": 1.4, "saturated_fat_g": 0.2, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 0.0, "sodium_mg": 12.7, "fiber_g": 5.3, "sugar_g": 4.1, "unsaturated_fat_g": 1.1, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": ["high fiber", "low-fat", "vegan", "vegetarian"], "course": [], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["champagne vinegar", "chive", "cilantro", "easy", "lime", "low calorie", "radicchio", "salad", "sun-dried tomato", "weeknight"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 3.0, "count": 11}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1993-03-07", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T00:54:18.212898+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "jicama-relish-in-chilpotle-marinade", "nyt_id": 3631, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/3631-jicama-relish-in-chilpotle-marinade", "name": "Jicama Relish In Chilpotle Marinade", "author": "Regina Schrambling", "description": "Regina Schrambling", "servings": {"text": "About six cups", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "volume"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 25, "raw": {"total": "25 minutes, plus overnight refrigeration"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 medium jicama, about 1 pound (see note)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium jicama", "preparation": "about 1 pound (see note)", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 large carrot", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large carrot", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 medium zucchini", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium zucchini", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 to 3 pickled chilpotle peppers in an adobo sauce with their liquid (see note)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": 3.0, "unit": null, "item": "pickled chilpotle peppers in an adobo sauce with their liquid (see note)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 cup finely chopped onion", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "finely chopped onion", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "4 garlic cloves, peeled and minced", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "garlic cloves", "preparation": "peeled and minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 bay leaf", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "bay leaf", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "6 whole black peppercorns", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "whole black peppercorns", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "½ cup white vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "white vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "½ cup water", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "water", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "⅓ cup olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 0.3333333333333333, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "2 tablespoons chopped cilantro", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped cilantro", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "1 teaspoon good-quality dried oregano", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "good-quality dried oregano", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "Salt to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Using a knife, remove the skin from the jicama. Cut the flesh into half-inch dice. Place in a glass or earthenware bowl."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Peel the carrot. Bring a pot of water to a rolling boil and drop the carrot in. Let the water return to the boil, then remove the carrot and discard the water. When the carrot is cool enough to handle, cut it into half-inch dice. Add to the bowl with the jicama."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Scrub the zucchini well but do not peel it. Trim, then cut it into half-inch dice and add it to the bowl."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Drain the chilpotles, reserving the pickling sauce (use one chili for a relatively mild marinade; three will be stinging hot). Cut the chilies open lengthwise and scrape out the seeds (if your fingers are sensitive, you may want to wear rubber gloves). Finely chop the chilies and place them in a separate, medium-sized bowl."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Add the onion, garlic, bay leaf, peppercorns, vinegar, water, olive oil and cilantro to the chilpotle in the bowl. Blend in the reserved chilpotle sauce. Crumble the oregano between your fingers into the bowl. Whisk all the ingredients together, then pour the marinade over the jicama mixture. Toss the vegetables with the marinade to coat them completely. Add salt to taste."}, {"position": 6, "text": "Cover the relish and refrigerate for at least four hours, preferably overnight. Serve as an accompaniment to grilled meats or fish."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 259.3, "protein_g": 2.9, "carbohydrates_g": 21.7, "fat_g": 18.5, "saturated_fat_g": 2.6, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 0.0, "sodium_mg": 839.5, "fiber_g": 8.7, "sugar_g": 7.3, "unsaturated_fat_g": 15.2, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["mexican"], "diet": ["dairy-free", "gluten-free", "vegan", "vegetarian"], "course": ["side dish"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["boil", "chipotle chile", "condiments", "marinate"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 3.0, "count": 7}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1988-10-09", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T05:22:11.448656+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "jiggling-fruit-mold-with-berry-compote", "nyt_id": 5786, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/5786-jiggling-fruit-mold-with-berry-compote", "name": "Jiggling Fruit Mold With Berry Compote", "author": "Suzanne Hamlin", "description": "Suzanne Hamlin", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 75, "raw": {"total": "1 hour 15 minutes plus chilling time"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "4 cups (2 pints) raspberries or strawberries, hulled and sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "(2 pints) raspberries or strawberries", "preparation": "hulled and sliced", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 cups water", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "water", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "½ cup granulated sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "granulated sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "Pinch of salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "pinch of salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "4 sheets of gelatin or 1 tablespoon powdered unflavored gelatin", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "sheet", "item": "of gelatin or 1 tablespoon powdered unflavored gelatin", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "3 cups (1 ½ pints) mixed berries like blueberries, blackberries, raspberries and strawberries", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "(1 ½ pints) mixed berries like blueberries", "preparation": "blackberries, raspberries and strawberries", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ cup sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "½ cup water", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "water", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 tablespoon finely grated orange rind", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "finely grated orange rind", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "Pinch of salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "pinch of salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "½ cup unsweetened heavy cream, whipped", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "unsweetened heavy cream", "preparation": "whipped", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "To make the fruit jell, put the berries, water, sugar and salt in a saucepan. Bring to a boil, stirring, and boil gently for 3 or 4 minutes. Remove from the heat, and set aside for an hour."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Line a fine-meshed sieve with a double layer of cheesecloth, and strain the cooked berries, pressing down gently so no pulp or seeds get into the liquid. Discard the pulp; there should be 2 cups of berry juice."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Soften the gelatin sheets in enough cold water to cover for about 5 minutes. If using powdered gelatin, sprinkle it over ¼ cup cold water, and allow to soften for 5 minutes."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Put the reserved berry juice in a saucepan. Squeeze out excess water from the gelatin sheets, and add them to the juice, or add all the softened powdered gelatin. Warm over low heat, stirring, until the gelatin dissolves."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Spray four ½-cup molds with flavorless oil. (You can use metal molds, ramekins or coffee cups.) Fill with the berry juice. Refrigerate, covered, for 4 hours or overnight."}, {"position": 6, "text": "To make the berry compote, put the 1 ½ pints of mixed berries in a saucepan with the water, sugar, orange rind and salt. Bring to a low boil, and cook, stirring, for 3 to 4 minutes until the fruit has almost dissolved and is syrupy. Remove from the heat, transfer to a bowl, cool, and refrigerate, covered, for 4 hours or overnight."}, {"position": 7, "text": "To serve, spoon berry compote onto four dessert plates. Dip the bottom of each mold into warm water, and unmold onto the compote. Put a dollop of whipped cream on the side of each, and serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 445.0, "protein_g": 8.7, "carbohydrates_g": 81.0, "fat_g": 12.4, "saturated_fat_g": 6.9, "trans_fat_g": 0.4, "cholesterol_mg": 33.6, "sodium_mg": 101.7, "fiber_g": 16.4, "sugar_g": 61.9, "unsaturated_fat_g": 4.3, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["dessert", "side dish"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["berry", "boil", "gelatin"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 11}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1997-05-14", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T07:50:46.835642+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
